25","reason":"Let k be the vertical change along the edge joining the two upper blocks. For |k| = 0,1,2,3,4, the respective counts are 85,44,19,6,1, found by summing squared triangular multiplicities for 5 - |k| coordinate choices. Both tilt signs occur when k ≠ 0, giving 85 + 2(44 + 19 + 6 + 1) = 225.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_136"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_12B_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_174","cnm_191","cnm_h231"],"id":"upper-side-rise","label":"Count by the rise of the upper side","methodDirectNodeIds":{"upper-side-rise":["cnm_h232","math:lattice-counting","cnm_245","cnm_h087","cnm_136"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h232","math:lattice-counting","cnm_245","cnm_h087","cnm_136","cnm_174","cnm_191","cnm_h231"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"alignmentIds":["alignment:098a31a6568ab2ce566a46cf"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, π+2","reason":"In the first quadrant, (x-1/2)²+(y-1/2)²=1/2 gives the outer semicircle joining (1,0) to (0,1). The central diamond has area 2, and the four semicircles contribute 4·(π/4)=π. The isolated origin does not affect the area.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_136"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2016_AMC_10B_Q21","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["math:completing-square-expression","cnm_h176","cnm_p148","cnm_p192"],"id":"quadrant-semicircle-decomposition","label":"Identify the circular arcs in each quadrant","methodDirectNodeIds":{"quadrant-semicircle-decomposition":["cnm_p150","cnm_h177","cnm_008","cnm_136"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p150","cnm_h177","cnm_008","cnm_136","math:completing-square-expression","cnm_h176","cnm_p148","cnm_p192"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"alignmentIds":["alignment:098a31a6568ab2ce566a46cf"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B (π+2)","reason":"In the first quadrant, (x-1/2)²+(y-1/2)²=1/